-- DB update 2026_09_10_07 -> 2026_09_10_08
-- Arcane Mage rework (docs/arcane-mage-rework-design.md) - Phase 3, Batch C.
-- .claude/skills/class-rework/SKILL.md Phase 3: 4 more "Deferred to Phase 3" items (see plan at
-- the time: ~/.claude/plans/twinkling-strolling-lagoon.md).
--
-- Data half: real spell 44425 (Arcane Barrage) gets chain_targets raised 0 -> 5 (1 primary + up to
-- 4 stacks of Arcane Blast) so spell_mage_arcane_barrage can trim the natively chain-selected
-- target list down to the live stack count at cast time. Incanter's Absorption (44394-44396) gets
-- native proc scaffolding (ProcTypeMask 65536/ProcChance 100/ProcCharges 0) added to its existing
-- SPELL_AURA_DUMMY effect1 - unaffected by the existing passive read
-- (spell_mage_incanters_absorbtion_base_AuraScript, ProcCharges 0 = never consumed) - plus a
-- capstone marker (rank 3/44396 only, new effect3). Spellblade (200072-200074, Phase 1) gets the
-- same proc scaffolding (ProcTypeMask 4 = melee auto attack, ProcChance rank-scaled 4/8/12).
-- 3 new spells: 200085 ("Arcane Mastery", the shared Arcane Concentration/Missile Barrage Mastery
-- marker), 200086 ("Incanter's Absorption", the new shield proc buff), 200087 ("Spellblade", the
-- mana-restore trigger).
--
-- C++ half (src/server/scripts/Spells/spell_mage.cpp, src/server/game/Entities/Unit/
-- MageMechanics.cpp) ships alongside this migration, not through generate.py - see that diff.
-- Highlights: Missile Barrage's CheckProc (spell_mage_missile_barrage) rewritten from "Arcane Blast
-- full chance, any other cast 50%" to the design's actual named spell list (Starfire full chance;
-- Arcane Barrage/Fireball/Frostbolt/Slow/Moonfire half chance - Starsurge omitted, doesn't exist in
-- this WotLK ruleset). Arcane Concentration and Missile Barrage's shared Mastery clause is granted
-- inside spell_mage_clearcasting/spell_mage_missile_barrage_proc's own CheckProc (not a live
-- MageMechanics.cpp read - both can empower channeled Arcane Missiles, whose buff-consumption
-- happens before any tick's damage calc, see Batch A's Progress notes) and read via a short-lived
-- marker aura, consumed immediately once read.
--
-- Not yet resolved: whether Arcane Missiles/Arcane Overload should also drop the caster's Arcane
-- Blast stacks on cast (System Rulings implies Overload "behaves...exactly as Arcane Missiles does"
-- but nothing in the design's own Missile Barrage prose says Missiles drops stacks, and nothing
-- pulled from real data confirms it either) - left as the flagged nuance from Batch A, still open,
-- likely to be settled when Arcane Overload's own cast script is built (Batch D).
--
-- generate.py clean (zero lint WARNINGs). codestyle-cpp.py clean on both edited C++ files.
-- test_sql_dump.py + manual balanced-statement scan clean - codestyle-sql.py itself can't run in
-- this sandbox (no network for git fetch), same accepted limitation as every prior batch.

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (44425, 44394, 44395, 44396, 200072, 200073, 200074, 200085, 200086, 200087);
